{"skill":{"slug":"industry-research-report","displayName":"Industry Research Agent"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1776424711133,"changelog":"Publish 1.0.3","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":4868,"sha256":"3e3de54702431d0eb291900852b6d799053e0ea072f109b1c3505eeb1d34094a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/get_data.py","size":10224,"sha256":"d49bc507d935d4cf203519a824b4520e630e53314a18f2a0bb96dfa22896cabd","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2169,"sha256":"cb85cf9bc10eae821c898ca0637daf8211df7f6acd7b8d942278ab676951f9ba","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789438455910,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"a7b1f0393fb5464abdf5841affa0db088bc07dded5eb7c22bca96f8c6b985172","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/a7b1f0393fb5464abdf5841affa0db088bc07dded5eb7c22bca96f8c6b985172","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086697924},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":39,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":5,"checkedAt":1789438455910},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill appears to do what it says, but it downloads and stores remote report files and installs an unpinned dependency in ways that need careful review before use.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The script posts the user query and EM_API_KEY to a fixed remote service and saves returned PDF/DOCX attachments, but it does not bound response size, decoded attachment size, storage use, or DOCX decompression work.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill installs httpx without a version pin or hash and also documents pip3 install httpx --user, which can mutate the user's Python environment with unreviewed future dependency versions.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The activation language is broad enough to run the network-backed script for general deep industry analysis requests, and the skill does not require explicit confirmation before using the API key, making external calls, and writing files.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No background service, autostart hook, privilege escalation, memory write, or cross-session backdoor was found; persistence is limited to installed Python dependency state and generated report files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose, API-key use, fixed East Money endpoint, report generation, and local PDF/DOCX output are coherent and disclosed for an industry research report skill.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only in a trusted environment with a scoped EM_API_KEY. Prefer an isolated virtual environment, pin dependencies yourself, set INDUSTRY_RESEARCH_REPORT_OUTPUT_DIR to a controlled location, and treat generated attachments and share links as untrusted remote content until verified.","findings":"[LP3] expected: Script execution, env secret use, network access, and report file output are expected for the skill's purpose, but explicit runtime scoping would reduce unnecessary blast radius.\n[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad trigger could cause the skill to run for ordinary industry analysis where the user may not expect API-key use, network access, and local file generation.\n[SQP-3] expected: Chinese-only instructions and messages are visible in the artifact and are not security-malicious, but users should know the skill is primarily localized for Chinese use.\n[SDI-4] unexpected: The stock-screening example in the argparse help text conflicts with the industry-report purpose, but the executable behavior otherwise targets the industry report endpoint.\n[T08] unexpected: The unpinned httpx install is a real supply-chain concern because dependency code may differ from what was reviewed and is installed into the user environment.\n[T09] unexpected: The remote PDF/DOCX handling findings are supported by the code: base64 attachments and DOCX XML are decoded or decompressed without size, type, or quota checks.\n[T09] expected: Returning the remote share URL is expected for the report workflow and is disclosed, but users should treat the link as untrusted because the code does not validate its scheme or host.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789438455910}}}}}